        {
          "type": "reading",
          "text_en": "In Hadramout, every season has its work. In summer, in July and August, it is very hot in the valley. This is the date harvest. Farmers climb the palm trees and cut the dates. In autumn, in October and November, the beekeepers of Wadi Doan are very busy. The sidr trees have flowers, and the bees make the famous sidr honey. In winter, in December and January, the weather is cool in the valley. Many families visit their relatives. On the coast, from January to June, sea turtles come to Sharma beach. The school year usually starts in September and ends in June. The summer holiday is long, so many students help their families at work.",
